    "advisory": "Delhi: Some smoke may reach the city (risk MODERATE).\nSmoke from upwind crop fires is expected to start arriving in about 6 h, mostly between 6 h and 23 h from now (9 of 12 active fire clusters are upwind).\nSuggested actions:\n- Move strenuous outdoor sports and long assemblies indoors during the arrival window\n- Allow students with asthma to stay indoors and keep their inhalers at hand\nAir mixing: air is expected to mix poorly over the next 48 hours. Low boundary layer and weak winds let pollution from all sources, smoke included, build up near the ground, mostly at night and in the morning.\n- Prefer midday or afternoon for outdoor activity over early morning and evening\nThis is a forecast estimate, not medical advice.",
